_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5d1877d14bf21fc4793db1bcb258f8ad67474ec6" commit="c0028767b2c6922f964bda255dad728c0f8ea008" commit_message="kerberos: Add account manager  Adds the boilerplate for the Kerberos account manager  BUG=chromium:932075 TEST=Emerges  Change-Id: I5d1877d14bf21fc4793db1bcb258f8ad67474ec6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1473071 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1473071" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/71/1473071/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I8168f5451b61ae8d13cfd66d4924623990c506be" commit="ba3da93b80d2b5691b4f4900adb94bac6ab99f42" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Fix Bluetooth controller event mask config during system suspend  As part of CL:1383763, a few Bluetooth controller events were disabled on suspension, to prevent the system from waking up spuriously. This change is applying the same event mask change as in CL:1383763, but instead of overriding the entire set of events mask it selectively masks out or restores the required events during suspend and resume. In addition, the new Set Event Mask operation introduced in this change is using the BlueZ/NewBlue new suspend and resume infrastucture.  As part of suspend/resume operations, BlueZ sends a new MGMT command to the kernel to mask out/restore BT specified events. The kernel adds new functions to handle the Set Event Mask request. The request contains a value and mask parameters to enable overriding only selected events.  This change is for kerenl v4.4 only.  For more details on the Bluetooth/NewBlue suspend infra refer to CL:1454328  BUG=chromium:930973 TEST=suspend and resume of system and verify event mask is set properly by the kernel. Verify event mask HCI and MGMT messages in BTMON. Signed-off-by: Yoni Shavit &lt;yshavit@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I8168f5451b61ae8d13cfd66d4924623990c506be Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1464385 Commit-Ready: Yoni Shavit &lt;yshavit@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yoni Shavit &lt;yshavit@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1464385" owner_email="yshavit@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/85/1464385/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Iba36be1bd32f1443960d8913929d4cee98790931" commit="e9d6b8310a060067338f8a750d78ef3cc83b75c5" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: Normalize 3.14 kernel config  Run `./chromeos/scripts/kernelconfig olddefconfig`.  CONFIG_BT_HCI_LE_SPLITTER comes from commit d93f2d00736a (&quot;CHROMIUM: Bluetooth: Add BT splitter&quot;)  CONFIG_MEMCG changes come from commit 4c29f5871148 (&quot;CHROMIUM: config: turn off unused configs on x86_64 boards&quot;)  CONFIG_MALI_* changes come from commit 00d5f016a1ba (&quot;CHROMIUM: mali: update kbase to r26p0&quot;)  CONFIG_DRM* and CONFIG_FB* changes most likely come from commit 2050d95498db (&quot;drm/evdi: remove dependency on CONFIG_FB&quot;)  CONFIG_BRIDGE* changes come from commit 2e1582576518 (&quot;kernelv3.14: Enable ebtables modules&quot;)  BUG=None TEST=Build and boot on samus.  Change-Id: Iba36be1bd32f1443960d8913929d4cee98790931 Signed-off-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1478218 Commit-Ready: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kuo-Hsin Yang &lt;vovoy@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1478218" owner_email="kirtika@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/18/1478218/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I881f3505300cadf1e0b8dd1750bae4cf2876e514" commit="d25282cd4982aa8a6084e625945c6d3a005c266b" commit_message="ish: update power rail request (vnn)  When the AP is trying to go down to S0ix from S0 (suspend), we need to ensure that the ISH is not holding on to any power requests which would prevent the AP from transitioning to S0ix. Re-assert power request when AP enters resume back to S0.  Ultimately, the VNN will be controlled at a much finer grain once more power management features are introduces here for the ISH.  BRANCH=none BUG=b:123890178 TEST=run &quot;suspend_stress_test -c [loop#]&quot;, and pass; this is workaround to fix this issue so not blocking S0ix test.  Change-Id: I881f3505300cadf1e0b8dd1750bae4cf2876e514 Signed-off-by: li feng &lt;li1.feng@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jett Rink &lt;jettrink@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1461665 Reviewed-by: Edward Hill &lt;ecgh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1461665" owner_email="li1.feng@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/65/1461665/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.14" change_id="I418f2b70c3de76d0c59e7f278107eba4b5d80ba2" commit="a08c94b8219e19c37ab21bcc480ffa71828125f9" commit_message="UPSTREAM: perf/core: Fix impossible ring-buffer sizes warning  The following commit:    9dff0aa95a32 (&quot;perf/core: Don't WARN() for impossible ring-buffer sizes&quot;)  results in perf recording failures with larger mmap areas:    root@skl:/tmp# perf record -g -a   failed to mmap with 12 (Cannot allocate memory)  The root cause is that the following condition is buggy:   if (order_base_2(size) &gt;= MAX_ORDER)   goto fail;  The problem is that @size is in bytes and MAX_ORDER is in pages, so the right test is:   if (order_base_2(size) &gt;= PAGE_SHIFT+MAX_ORDER)   goto fail;  Fix it.  Reported-by: &quot;Jin, Yao&quot; &lt;yao.jin@linux.intel.com&gt; Bisected-by: Borislav Petkov &lt;bp@alien8.de&gt; Analyzed-by: Peter Zijlstra &lt;peterz@infradead.org&gt; Cc: Julien Thierry &lt;julien.thierry@arm.com&gt; Cc: Mark Rutland &lt;mark.rutland@arm.com&gt; Cc: Alexander Shishkin &lt;alexander.shishkin@linux.intel.com&gt; Cc: Arnaldo Carvalho de Melo &lt;acme@redhat.com&gt; Cc: Jiri Olsa &lt;jolsa@redhat.com&gt; Cc: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt; Cc: Namhyung Kim &lt;namhyung@kernel.org&gt; Cc: Peter Zijlstra &lt;peterz@infradead.org&gt; Cc: Thomas Gleixner &lt;tglx@linutronix.de&gt; Cc: Greg Kroah-Hartman &lt;gregkh@linuxfoundation.org&gt; Cc: &lt;stable@vger.kernel.org&gt; Fixes: 9dff0aa95a32 (&quot;perf/core: Don't WARN() for impossible ring-buffer sizes&quot;) Signed-off-by: Ingo Molnar &lt;mingo@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 528871b456026e6127d95b1b2bd8e3a003dc1614)  BUG=b:124795843 TEST=perf record -g -a  Change-Id: I418f2b70c3de76d0c59e7f278107eba4b5d80ba2 Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1478048 Reviewed-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Yu Zhao &lt;yuzhao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alexey Alexandrov &lt;aalexand@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1478048" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/48/1478048/1"